{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"decfc102723d3a4a","type":"group","x":-790,"y":-229,"width":1660,"height":1949,"label":"RAT Modding"},
		{"id":"1510b52db4fc12cf","x":960,"y":-120,"width":1080,"height":1080,"type":"group","label":"bass modding"},
		{"id":"953650432611cf82","type":"group","x":-705,"y":-560,"width":1490,"height":265,"label":"pedalboard"},
		{"id":"4b08e5b963502f53","type":"group","x":980,"y":-780,"width":290,"height":540,"label":"instruments"},
		{"id":"b96635cb6de17c3e","type":"group","x":-1140,"y":-580,"width":290,"height":305,"label":"amp setup"},
		{"id":"04ecca745aa0bf96","type":"text","text":"trying to make a bold move and also swap out the transistor in the op-amp so that it could have a brighter or darker sound to it.","x":-180,"y":145,"width":250,"height":150},
		{"id":"140ced726c51d0f7","type":"text","text":"this is something where I am really fighting with because this may have huge changes to the circuitry like removing a resistor. I will look for it and see what is the easiest to be done.","x":-400,"y":380,"width":250,"height":217},
		{"id":"98acb759fb852357","type":"text","text":"f#%ck 'em, I'm going to do it","x":-560,"y":940,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"28804f94429a9b22","type":"text","text":"so no diode stacking :(","x":-560,"y":1560,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"8d5b0183513fb359","type":"text","text":"so first I'm going to modify a RAT 2 pedal to make my sound more aggressive.","x":3,"y":-149,"width":250,"height":89},
		{"id":"68372c44bf1c5893","type":"text","text":"chorus (obtained)","x":-385,"y":-540,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"70cf081d8e4ca70d","type":"text","text":"so in the D1 diode position I'm going to keep the original Si diode in there and stack it with an LED so it has a massive input boost, then I'm going to shoot all that massive volume into a Ge diode and a Schottky diode in the D2 position stacked, so it completely  f@&king smashes that high volume in a tiny space where it compresses heavily resulting in a very harsh asymmetrical distortion.","x":360,"y":660,"width":250,"height":408},
		{"id":"7a8fad2d55c2f7ae","type":"text","text":"I decide to build one from scratch :D","x":520,"y":1300,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5beb323eec020bef","type":"text","text":"Houston we have a problem... so with the diode combination does work but it's not optimal, the Si-LED combination would have so much headroom that it would go into a light distortion while the \nGe-Schottky would be fighting for it's life. so i am going to put in D1 a Ge diode and in D2 a Schottky diode to still have asymmetrical clipping but that it has lower headroom for more compression, harsher clipping and voltage leaking for even more disgusting sounds","x":-59,"y":1199,"width":250,"height":501},
		{"id":"f6b94ceae6df236e","type":"text","text":"compressor","x":215,"y":-540,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"24b1593374a4bed3","type":"text","text":"modded ProCo RAT 2","x":-85,"y":-385,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"61ea1a99b641dcf8","type":"text","text":"Joyo scylla","x":215,"y":-385,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"fc878b666f6cfaf7","type":"text","text":"Korg pitchblack XS bass","x":515,"y":-385,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"5c795f62c9bd4fe4","type":"text","text":"NUX analog chorus","x":-385,"y":-385,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"67ce56c9782f95e0","type":"text","text":"modded Sterling stingray2\n(C standard to B standard)","x":1000,"y":-340,"width":250,"height":80},
		{"id":"4e44e59028c2314c","type":"text","text":"tuner pedal","x":515,"y":-540,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d8a26946199ce9e4","type":"text","text":"distortion","x":-85,"y":-540,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"e354b515c8f9b984","type":"text","text":"searching first the clipping diodes where I want to make it more like a sputtery old school 50's/60's psychedelic distortion/fuzz hybrid but more compatible for bass like the RAT pedal is.","x":200,"y":111,"width":250,"height":209},
		{"id":"41e54a069f3724f0","type":"text","text":"diode stacking it is!","x":300,"y":480,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"8306971e5b1e2561","type":"text","text":"my home built explorer\n(D standard)","x":1000,"y":-550,"width":250,"height":80},
		{"id":"b46d64bef2755f4e","type":"text","text":"equalizer","x":-685,"y":-540,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"3e596d8415e9f4f3","type":"text","text":"Behringer BEQ700","x":-685,"y":-385,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"201882c2f79e3729","type":"text","text":"name for it is pending...","x":-520,"y":-209,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"842d70682910105f","type":"text","text":"if I would do it, it will be a TL071 chip because it could be a drop-in replacement and it would make it even more aggressive with the diode stacking.","x":-160,"y":720,"width":250,"height":190},
		{"id":"d229d141d4d1f1cf","type":"text","text":"inspirations are a fuzz face, a tone bender and a big muff Ge4.","x":600,"y":-40,"width":250,"height":103},
		{"id":"4b2bd48ca8cb947d","type":"text","text":"TC electronic BAM200","x":-1120,"y":-565,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"bda7a9c3b9ceb64e","type":"text","text":"TC electronic BC208","x":-1120,"y":-355,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"a829f2d384f9fb68","type":"text","text":"this is getting close to be done","x":-1303,"y":538,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0244d0c1eba6a39e","type":"text","text":"possible names:\n- Nurgle (warhammer\n- reference)\n- Black death (the pedal color itself is black and rats spreaded the plague)\n- Mutagen (TMNT reference)\n- Murloc (WoW reference)\n- Eraticate (rat mixed with eradicate)\n- Stuart little (just very funny)\n- Twitch (LoL reference)\n- Chuckee (chuck e. cheese reference)\n- Roadkill (just sounds really cool)\n- Argus (a niche Dutch reference)\n","x":-770,"y":40,"width":250,"height":600},
		{"id":"e12d2cd473a439f1","type":"text","text":"maybe the baritone guitar i built (B standard)","x":1000,"y":-760,"width":250,"height":80},
		{"id":"a9dba28175c0f260","x":1000,"y":-440,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"now an Ibanez tmb30"},
		{"id":"fae3899bd1882e33","x":1531,"y":98,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"the bass in question"},
		{"id":"508bb168ec513dc6","x":980,"y":300,"width":250,"height":640,"type":"text","text":"because everything is already really good on this bass, the changes are minimal:\n- a lace pickups aluma j bass coil\n- remove the p coil and the volume with it\n- remove the tone knob\n- a toggle kill switch in the position of the tone knob\n- a green acrylic             see-through sheet (for over the p coil cavity)\n- a green fender amp jewel in the open volume knob hole because i am not using it\n\nI will use ernie ball short scale slinky's which are 045.-105."},
		{"id":"f8b837fbebdcbd34","x":1620,"y":380,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"file","file":"static_files/TMB30-Black-full-1024x1024-2735275975.webp"},
		{"id":"45f35a7bd4e7b5d4","x":1160,"y":-100,"width":250,"height":280,"type":"text","text":"okay so slight change... I have a very beautiful Ibanez tmb30 bass in black which was already perfect for the job style and playing wise for what i want to make while i can still keep my idol as inspiration for it. here bellow what I'm going to do with it."},
		{"id":"73f0788334d346bd","x":1300,"y":520,"width":250,"height":168,"type":"text","text":"it's name will be 'abjection' because it's a super depressing name for it and that's my goal with my music like Type O-negative"}
	],
